{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdRtj6JC1q8hc95AGrSy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Wr73twaLLXoRxLBkfJEzE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_4\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `complement_symmetry_aversion`: each sequence's apparent randomness is still judged by its switching rate against a personal ideal (lenient toward over-alternation), personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry, complement symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch, and people still guess at a personal rate. The one change is where people's consistency differs: instead of a personal sensitivity to the switching rate alone, each person has their own overall decisiveness (drawn from a population) that sharpens or flattens the whole comparison of the two impressions, so some people follow every cue of the shared impression almost deterministically while others follow all of them weakly — addressing the critique (surviving FDR) that people differ in how often they agree with the majority choice more than the incumbent produces.\nEOF\necho personal_decisiveness_complement_symmetry > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc = open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/complement_symmetry_aversion.py\").read()\ndoc_old = src.split('\"\"\"')[1]\ndoc_new = \"\"\"Personal decisiveness on top of complement-symmetry aversion.\n\nRefinement of `complement_symmetry_aversion`: each sequence's apparent\nrandomness is still judged by its switching rate against a personal ideal\n(lenient toward over-alternation), personal weights on imbalance and the\nlongest run, shared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry, complement\nsymmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch, plus a personal\nlapse rate. The one change: the personal sensitivity no longer applies to the\nswitching-rate penalty alone; alternation sensitivity is shared and each person\nhas an overall decisiveness that scales the whole difference between the two\nimpressions, so people differ in how consistently they follow the common\nimpression (the critique's excess spread in majority agreement).\n\"\"\"\nsrc = src.replace(doc_old, doc_new, 1)\nold_beta = '''    # Personal alternation sensitivity (non-centred log-normal population).\n    mu_beta = pm.Normal(\"mu_beta\", mu=2.5, sigma=0.5)\n    sigma_beta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_beta\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_beta = pm.Normal(\"z_beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    beta = pm.math.exp(mu_beta + sigma_beta * z_beta)\n'''\nnew_beta = '''    # Shared alternation sensitivity.\n    mu_beta = pm.Normal(\"mu_beta\", mu=2.5, sigma=0.5)\n    beta = pm.math.exp(mu_beta)\n\n    # Personal overall decisiveness (log-normal, median 1): scales the whole comparison.\n    sigma_dec = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_dec\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_dec = pm.Normal(\"z_dec\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    decisiveness = pm.math.exp(sigma_dec * z_dec)\n'''\nassert old_beta in src\nsrc = src.replace(old_beta, new_beta)\nsrc = src.replace(\"    b = beta[participant_id]\\n\", \"    b = beta\\n    s = decisiveness[participant_id]\\n\")\nsrc = src.replace(\"p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b)\", \"p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(s * (score_a - score_b))\")\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_4/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"decis\\|b = beta\\|p_engaged\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":84798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":676,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6ac9792-9179-4746-be24-f102e24a914d","uuid":"25dec187-3af4-404a-b9fb-cc7b66aa0e73","timestamp":"2026-10-02T12:43:28.006Z","request_id":"req_011CfdRtifjqZnEzNrb6cxCH"}
